      "writtenOn": "2016-10-12T04:15:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "space things out:\n\nThis patch improves check_token validation performance by only pulling revocation events based on the token `issued_at` value, taking advantage of the table index. In this way, only a subset of relevant events will be returned for validation.\n\n\nBenchmarks can be seen at [1] but included here as well:\n\n\nTime per Request for Old Method\n---------------------------------\n10 revokes at 7.908ms\n100 revokes at 18.224ms\n1,000 revokes at 110.155ms\n10,000 revokes at 1998.220ms\n\n\nTime per Request for New Method\n----------------------------------\n10 revokes at 17.636ms\n100 revokes at 17.279ms\n1,000 revokes at 17.370ms\n10,000 revokes w/all revokes issued before token at 17.263ms (best case)\n10,000 revokes w/all revokes after token creation 44.934ms (worst case)\n\n[1] https://gist.github.com/csrichard1/4b7b8527ee5a6565a84956cff33cf29b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "358a90712dfb420a83ffe1f9c19c7832441e9d32",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
