      "writtenOn": "2016-10-11T16:12:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this section be an else/if statement? Can a token have a user/trustee/trustor all populated at once? \n\n  # populate user for query\n  if \u0027user\u0027 in token:\n      user.append(RevocationEvent.user_id \u003d\u003d token[\u0027user_id\u0027])\n  elif \u0027trustor_id\u0027 in token:\n      user.append(RevocationEvent.user_id \u003d\u003d token[\u0027trustor_id\u0027])\n  elif \u0027trustee_id\u0027 in token:\n      user.append(RevocationEvent.user_id \u003d\u003d token[\u0027trustor_id\u0027])\n\n  # populate project for query if present\n  if \u0027project_id\u0027 in token:\n      proj.append(RevocationEvent.project_id \u003d\u003d token[\u0027project_id\u0027])\n \n  # populate audit information for query if present\n  if \u0027audit_id\u0027 in token:\n      audit.append(RevocationEvent.audit_id \u003d\u003d token[\u0027audit_id\u0027])",
      "revId": "358a90712dfb420a83ffe1f9c19c7832441e9d32",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
